    {
      "_why": [
        "«غير محدَّد» — the sector of an establishment that arrives through its till, and §4.2 says",
        "it never sees the sector screen at all: its catalogue is built from its own invoices, and",
        "asking a partner to pick a trade on its customer's behalf would be a guess written into",
        "somebody's data.",
        "",
        "IT EXISTS BECAUSE seed_tenant REFUSES AN UNKNOWN SECTOR, correctly — a typo must not silently",
        "produce an empty shop. Without a row to name, a partner provisioning an integrated shop had",
        "no legal value to send, so the honest answer is a sector that means 'not stated' rather than",
        "a flag that means 'skip the check'.",
        "",
        "NO FIELDS, and that is the whole point. `plate` on an unknown trade renders a vehicle input",
        "in what may be a salon; absent, the field screen asks only what every trade has. The catch-all",
        "is the single service, because an invoice line that matches nothing still has to land",
        "somewhere or the visit is lost.",
        "",
        "AND NO ASSET. The vehicle is the only asset in the product, and claiming one for a shop we",
        "cannot classify would attach cars to customers who do not have them."
      ],
      "key": "unspecified",
      "name": "غير محدَّد",
      "asset": "none",
      "fields": [],
      "sort": 900,
